  "report_period": "Week 42 (9th Oct to 16th Oct 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Golden Myrtalia\" 178/2011 SWS, China (SS/DD 10/2026) was committed to Norwegian interests at USD 40 mill basis SS/DD passed. For reference, the sister vessel \"Pigassos\" 176/2011 SWS, China (SS/DD 07/2026) was sold back in May at USD 31,7 mill. Following the sale of the Panamax \"Pabur\" 76/2012 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 12/2027, Ice Class 1C) back in April at USD 16,5 mill, Harren Bulkers have now committed the sister \"Pabal\" 76/2012 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 10/2027, Ice Class 1C) at rgn USD 17 mill. On the Handysize sector, Japanese owners committed their \"Locomotion\" 38/2013 Shimanami, Japan (SS 12/2030, DD 12/2028) at USD 19,8 mill. Remind you that back in July, the \"Sakura Dream\" 38/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 12/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold at USD 18,5 mill basis delivery Nov- Dec'26. Moreover, ZBB Bulkers committed their \"ZBB Serenity\" 37/2010 Huatai, China (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2028, Ice Class 1C) to Turkish compatriots at USD 12 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-younger \"CS Calla\" 37/2011 Tianjin, China (SS/DD 10/2026, Ice Class 1C) was sold in September at low-mid USD 11 mill. In addition, Carsten Rehder committed the \"Lima Strait\" 37/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 07/2027) at USD 15,2 mill. Note that in June, the sister vessel \"Maple Marina\" 37/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 10/2027) was sold at USD 14,3 mill.",
    "tankers": "Andriaki Shipping have committed their Suezmax \"Nicolaos\" 164/2010 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 01/2030, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted) at USD 90,8 mill and the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Militos\" 164/2012 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 04/2027) at USD 95,5 mill. Note that a month ago, the sister vessel \"Stella\" 164/2011 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 04/2031, DD 05/2029) was sold at xs USD 80 mill. Furthermore, the \"Yellow Trader\" 158/2004 Daewoo, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027) was committed at USD 61 mill, while the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Nordic Freedom\" 159/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS 03/2030, DD 04/2028) was committed a week ago at USD 65 mill. The LR1 \"Asian Phoenix\" 72/2006 Dalian, China (SS/DD due) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 20 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"VS Prospera\" 73/2005 New Century, China (SS 07/2029, DD 07/2027) was committed a couple of weeks ago at high USD 16 mill. The MR1 \"Easterly Jupiter\" 36/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 02/2029, DD 05/2027) was committed to Greek interests at USD 19 mill, while the sister vessel \"Easterly Symphony\" 36/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 11/2027) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 20 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route softened further, with Dampier to Qingdao fixtures settling between USD 11.25/13.40 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, fixed between USD 30.00/31.50 fio. Out of South Africa, Saldanha Bay departures to Qingdao achieved between USD 23.25/24.08 fio, while a TRMT run to Qingdao made USD 9.85 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan and West Coast India options settled between USD 20,000/23,500 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, India and Singapore-Japan ranges fetched between USD 19,000/27,000 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China, China and Japan ranges achieved between USD 16,000/23,500 pd. From West Coast India and East Coast India, trips via South Africa and ECSA to India and Singapore-Japan ranges fixed between USD 25,500/28,750 pd. In the Atlantic, a Continent trip via USG back to Continent/Med range made USD 21,500 pd, an East Med run via NCSA achieved USD 27,250 pd, and a Continent departure via NCSA to Singapore-Japan reached USD 32,000 pd. On period, fixtures for 2 laden legs up to 7 months duration were secured between USD 19,000/27,000 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal runs to South East Asia and ECI settled between USD 23,000/24,000 pd and USD 15,250 pd respectively. NoPac trips from North China and Japan to South East Asia fetched USD 25,000 pd, while South China clinker runs to ECI achieved strong levels between USD 30,000/31,000 pd. A long-haul departure from North China to West Africa fixed at USD 24,000 pd. Out of the Persian Gulf, a limestone trip to India obtained USD 16,500 pd, while a South Africa coal run to ECI reached USD 26,000 pd alongside a USD 260,000 ballast bonus. In the Mediterranean, salt to US Gulf and clinker to West Africa made USD 14,500 pd and USD 22,000 pd respectively. In the Atlantic, a US Gulf front-haul petcoke trip to China secured USD 34,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Pacific, regional departures from North China to South East Asia fixed at USD 19,000 pd, while a South East Asia coal run to Far East settled at USD 12,750 pd. A trip from South East Asia via Australia to China made USD 16,000 pd and a steel run from East Coast India to Continent obtained USD 13,500 pd. In the Atlantic, a US Gulf grain run to WCCA achieved USD 17,500 pd, an ECSA departure to Continent fixed at USD 15,000 pd alongside a USD 150,000 ballast bonus and an East Med trip to NCSA reached USD 11,000 pd."
    }
  },
